format 1
adapter feed 1
npc: npc-ray

post ft-ray-chest-daily
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"daily"}

text:
    Daily chest opened. Small reward. Same time tomorrow.

post ft-ray-chest-weekly
kind: celebrate
trigger: chest_opened
chip: quests
condition: {"period":"weekly"}

text:
    Weekly chest open. Every quest of the week done. Checked off.

post ft-ray-first-lesson
kind: celebrate
trigger: first_lesson
chip: lesson

text:
    First lesson done: “{lesson}”. Good. The next one is on the map.

post ft-ray-lesson-becquerel-gray-sievert-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"becquerel-gray-sievert"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Becquerel counts decays. Gray is energy absorbed. Sievert is potential for harm.

post ft-ray-lesson-becquerel-gray-sievert-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"becquerel-gray-sievert","perfect":true}

text:
    Perfect on “{lesson}”. Right unit, right question. Nothing mixed up.

post ft-ray-lesson-detecting-radiation-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"detecting-radiation"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Geiger counter, scintillation counter, dosimeter. Three tools, three jobs.

post ft-ray-lesson-detecting-radiation-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"detecting-radiation"}

text:
    A working detector picks up a little radiation almost anywhere. Background is always there. Remember it.

post ft-ray-lesson-ionizing-or-not-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"ionizing-or-not"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Radio waves, light, X-rays: all radiation. Only some can knock electrons off atoms. Noted.

post ft-ray-lesson-ionizing-or-not-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"ionizing-or-not"}

text:
    Sorted. Ionizing and non-ionizing are different things. Not all radiation is the same.

post ft-ray-lesson-irradiated-or-contaminated-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"irradiated-or-contaminated"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Exposure is not contamination. Radiation does not spread. The material does.

post ft-ray-lesson-irradiated-or-contaminated-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"irradiated-or-contaminated"}

text:
    Standing near a source is not the same as having material on you. Good. Keep them apart.

post ft-ray-lesson-what-stops-what-1
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"what-stops-what"}

text:
    “{lesson}” done. Paper stops alpha. Thin metal stops beta. Gamma needs thick, dense material. Checked off.

post ft-ray-lesson-what-stops-what-2
kind: celebrate
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: lesson
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"what-stops-what","perfect":true}

text:
    Perfect on “{lesson}”. Three kinds, three stoppers, no misses. Noted.

post ft-ray-quests
kind: celebrate
trigger: daily_quests_done
chip: quests

text:
    All daily quests done. Open the chest. That is the whole job for today.

post ft-ray-rank-passed
kind: celebrate
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed"}

text:
    You passed {rival} in the weekly ranking. Noted. Hold the spot.

post ft-ray-checkpoint-radiation-meets-matter
kind: milestone
trigger: checkpoint_pass
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter"}
reactors: npc-ada

text:
    The {unit} checkpoint is passed. Checked off.

post ft-ray-testout-radiation-meets-matter
kind: milestone
trigger: testout_pass
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter"}
reactors: npc-ada

text:
    You tested out of “{unit}”. You already knew it. Now it is on the record.

post ft-ray-unit-radiation-meets-matter-2
kind: milestone
trigger: unit_complete
chip: unit
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter"}
reactors: npc-ada

text:
    You finished “{unit}”. You know what is ionizing, what stops what, and which unit answers which question. Good. Mina is next.

post ft-ray-unit-radioactivity-1
kind: milestone
trigger: unit_complete
chip: unit
weight: 2
condition: {"unitId":"radioactivity"}
reactors: npc-ada

text:
    Someone just finished “{unit}” with Ada. They know why nuclei change. Now they find out what the radiation does to things. That part is mine.

post ft-ray-comeback-14
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":14}

text:
    Two weeks, {name}. Fine. Start with one lesson. Do not try to catch up all at once.

post ft-ray-comeback-3
kind: nudge
trigger: comeback
condition: {"minDays":3}

text:
    {name}. You are back. Pick up where you stopped. One lesson is enough.

post ft-ray-rank-passed-by
kind: nudge
trigger: rank_change
chip: ranks
condition: {"direction":"passed_by"}

text:
    {rival} passed you in the weekly ranking. One lesson fixes that. Go do it.

post ft-ray-tease-radiation-meets-matter
kind: tease
trigger: lesson_complete
chip: unit
condition: {"unitId":"radiation-meets-matter","lessonId":"detecting-radiation"}

text:
    Detecting is done. Next: units. Becquerel, gray, sievert. Three of them. Learn the difference.
